TurnPilot

TurnPilot is a fork of openpilot (https://github.com/commaai/openpilot). The fork as a whole is distributed under the GNU Affero General Public License, version 3. The full text is in LICENSE-AGPL-3.0.

The reason is the detector. TurnPilot finds pedestrians and cars with YOLO26 from Ultralytics (https://github.com/ultralytics/ultralytics). Its code and weights are AGPL-3.0, and so are models trained or exported with its code, so the combined work is distributed under AGPL-3.0.

Source: https://github.com/kaileh57/turnpilot

Parts, by license

openpilot, Copyright (c) 2018, Comma.ai, Inc., MIT. The notice is in LICENSE and stays. Code that came from openpilot keeps its MIT license, which allows it to be part of this AGPL-3.0 work. TurnPilot's edits to upstream files are AGPL-3.0.

TurnPilot's own code, AGPL-3.0:
  openpilot/selfdrive/turnpilot/
  openpilot/tools/turnpilot/
  openpilot/tools/sim/bridge/beamng/
  tools/turnpilot/
  docs/turnpilot/

YOLO26 models and what is built from them, AGPL-3.0, Copyright (c) Ultralytics:
  openpilot/selfdrive/turnpilot/models/ (yolo26n.onnx, yolo26s.onnx, export_yolo26.py)
