  Nothing that uses these files can go upstream to openpilot.

Submodules, under their own licenses: opendbc, panda, msgq, rednose and teleoprtc from comma.ai (MIT), and tinygrad (MIT).

Not in the repository, installed on the device:
  pyvalhalla and Valhalla (MIT, https://github.com/valhalla/valhalla), installed by tools/turnpilot/install_valhalla_device.sh.
  Map tiles built from OpenStreetMap extracts. The data is (c) OpenStreetMap contributors, under the Open Database License 1.0 (https://www.openstreetmap.org/copyright). Anything that shows a map or route made from the tiles has to credit OpenStreetMap.

The AGPL network clause

Section 13 of the AGPL applies to the phone app that turnpilot_web serves. If you modify TurnPilot and let other people use it over a network, the modified version has to offer them its source.
